{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_012fxyMZS4dN3XRviqy6F3Mc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary â€” `anchor_gui.py` (deliverables trio session)\n\n**Goal / what it is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is the primary Anchor application: a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that serves the interactive dashboard and exposes API endpoints so every UI action writes directly to the markdown source files, logs the change, and refreshes state (module docstring, lines 1â€“14).\n- Runnable directly (`python3 anchor_gui.py [--port 8777]`) and also imported by `anchor_healthcheck` (header guards against double log-handler attach when imported twice, lines 61â€“71).\n\n**Key structure (grounded in the defined functions/classes)**\n- **Paths & data dirs** resolve through the shared `paths` helper honoring `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`; a process-wide `WRITE_LOCK` is held around every markdown/JSON mutation to prevent lost updates under `ThreadingHTTPServer` (lines 27â€“47).\n- **Build identity / cache-bust**: `_compute_build_id()` uses `git rev-parse --short HEAD` (falling back to source mtime); `BUILD_ID` plus `_CACHE_BUST_JS_TEMPLATE` / `cache_bust_script()` drive self-healing client reloads that also unregister stale service workers and clear Cache Storage (lines 78â€“162).\n- **Markdown parsing/serialization**: `parse_tasks_from_md`, `serialize_task_line`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks`, and `gather_all()` (dedup across DASHBOARD.md + domains) read markdown into dicts (lines 181â€“387).\n- **WebSocket codec** (stdlib, hand-rolled RFC-6455): `ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `encode_close_frame`, `encode_pong_frame`, `decode_frames` for PTY terminal transport (lines 463â€“633).\n- **Traversal-safe static asset routes**: `anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, `brand_asset` plus an `_unsafe_path_seg` guard (lines 634â€“750).\n- **R&D project surface render helpers**: status line/dot, project tiles & rows, rollup toggle, effort cards, sessions, grass board, Kanban, lane sessions, and the large `render_project_window_html` (lines ~1024â€“3645) â€” the project \"cockpit\"/Mission-Control window.\n- **Change operations** (each wrapped via `_with_write_lock`): `mark_done`, `mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `link_task`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, `log_change` (lines 3885â€“4319).\n- **`generate_html`** (lines 4320â€“6269) builds the entire dashboard page as one HTML string with embedded CSS/JS.\n- **`AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)`** (line 6270) routes all GET/POST; on GET failure it logs and continues (line 7156).\n\n**API surface (grounded in the routing)**\n- Task/dashboard endpoints: `/api/status`, `/api/done`, `/api/undone`, `/api/add`, `/api/capture`, `/api/edit_task`, `/api/edit_project`, promote/demote task & project, `/api/cancel`, `/api/save_for_later`, `/api/restore`, `/api/heartbeat`.\n- R&D endpoints: project lifecycle (`new_project`/`open_project`/`rescan`/`set_priority`/`archive`/`future`/`retire`/`reactivate`/`set_notes`/`set_blurb`/`link_task`), deliverables (`run_deliverable`/`pin_deliverable`/`launch_deliverable`), lanes/gates (`launch_lane`/`answer_gate`), terminals (`start_terminal`/`term_input`/`term_discover`/`term_adopt`/`term_start`/`term_kill`/`term_set_engine`/`term_resize`/`term_input2`), previews (`preview_start`/`preview_stop`), `cancel_job`, `regenerate_summary`.\n- Read/GET data routes: `/report/`, `/summary/`, `/artifact/`, `/project/<id>`, `/api/rnd/handoff_proposal`, `session_summary`, `session_doc_roles`, `project_rollup`, `term_sessions`, `projects`, `dir_browse`, `tail`, `jobs`, `previews`, `term_stream`, plus KaTeX/xterm/brand/anchor-term static prefixes and favicon/icons.\n\n**Server lifecycle**\n- `make_server`/`_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` enforce a single-instance bind (Windows `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE`) so a duplicate process exits cleanly rather than racing on port 8777; `resolve_bind_host` defaults to loopback `127.0.0.1`; `_heartbeat_watchdog` and `main()` complete the runtime (lines 7930â€“8093).\n\n**Findings / notes**\n- No external dependencies in this file â€” Python stdlib only (`json, logging, os, re, socket, sys, threading, time, traceback, webbrowser, http.server, urllib`, lines 16â€“21); the lone native `pywinpty` exception lives in `pty_manager.py`, not here.\n- HTML is generated inside Python f-strings, so literal CSS/JS braces must be doubled (per project convention; the project-window JS is kept as a raw non-f string to avoid this).\n\n**Errors:** none observed in the source; the file is internally consistent (8,093 lines; all routes dispatch to defined handlers).\n\n(Claims above are grounded in the single member document `anchor_gui.py`; line references are from the current file.)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3307,"cache_read_input_tokens":53358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3307},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57b165ea-801c-4884-a9c5-829f186468e5","uuid":"4ae17952-702d-475f-a18f-ed0dd8b8e737","request_id":"req_011Cc1H6rupsx2vGJiBbUseE"}
